    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe placement is right and this is well-aligned with the codebase: `Owner` already hosts a family of \"derived at response time, not persisted\" computed getters (`getBulkSignupWarning`, `getHouseholdSize`, `getMembershipLevel`, `getLocality`, `getContactPreference`, `getCheckDigit`, `getIdentityKey`). `getAgeBand()` follows that exact convention \u2014 matching Javadoc style, null-guarding, computing against `registrationDate` \u2014 so a maintainer would find the unit natural. Nothing is duplicated, and the entity is not being turned into a catch-all beyond the pattern it already established. The schema and OpenAPI additions are consistent across all four DB dialects and the two schemas.\n\nOne concrete, actionable idiomatic nit:\n\n- `Owner.java:152` uses the fully-qualified `java.time.Period.between(...)` inline, while the rest of the file imports its `java.time` types (`import java.time.LocalDate;` at line 24, used unqualified everywhere including the adjacent `birthDate`/`registrationDate` fields). Add `import java.time.Period;` and reference `Period.between(...)` to match the file's established style.\n\nEverything else about the structure is clean.",
